// REJECTS: no viable alternative at input
//
// Constraint clause ORDER is fixed by the grammar, not stylistic:
//     ~owner? ~externalId? ~function ~enforcementLevel? ~message?
// with ~function the only required clause. This puts ~message first.
//
// Worth pinning because a hand-written recursive-descent parser naturally accepts clauses
// in any order -- you loop over "which clause is next" -- and would silently be MORE
// permissive than legend-engine. That kind of divergence never surfaces as a failure; it
// surfaces as a model that one engine loads and the other rejects.
###Pure
Class fixture::neg::Reordered
[
   backwards
   (
      ~message: 'this clause may not precede ~function'
      ~function: $this.code->length() > 2
   )
]
{
   code: String[1];
}
